{
 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "VO-01",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 7.916,
   "text": "You're a fiber cable from Chicago to New Jersey, an estimated three hundred million dollars of glass, and your whole job is saving three milliseconds."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-02",
   "start": 8.065,
   "end": 10.557,
   "text": "Wait, who pays that much for three milliseconds?"
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-03",
   "start": 10.706,
   "end": 17.169,
   "text": "Trading firms, because when a price moves in Chicago, they can react in New Jersey before a rival's order gets there."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-04",
   "start": 17.269,
   "end": 23.939,
   "text": "Older cables followed the railroads, but you cut the straightest path, making the round trip in about thirteen milliseconds in twenty ten."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-05",
   "start": 24.038,
   "end": 30.423,
   "text": "You're the fastest line around, until microwave towers beat you, because a signal through the air beats light through your glass."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-06",
   "start": 30.522,
   "end": 36.363,
   "text": "In twenty seventeen, Zayo agreed to buy the company that built you for one hundred twenty-seven million dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-07",
   "start": 36.462,
   "end": 42.717,
   "text": "And inside two New Jersey data centers, Cboe matches every cable's length, so no firm sitting closer gets a shorter wire."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-08",
   "start": 43.114,
   "end": 51.031,
   "text": "So does that mean regular people buying stocks are losing to you? Not if they hold for years, because three milliseconds barely matters over ten years."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-09",
   "start": 51.369,
   "end": 56.897,
   "text": "The cable was built for a sprint, but investing is a marathon, so which race are you running?"
  }
 ],
